      "body": "## Summary\n\n- preserve `HashTopK.topk` as the empty `topk_ids` and `topk_weights` width, including fused shared-expert columns\n- size the empty `router_logits` placeholder by `num_experts`, matching normal forward\n- remove the per-rank-only empty-column workaround now that both shared-slot policies use the same output contract\n- compare empty-helper output with the real zero-token torch forward in both per-rank and non-per-rank regression cases\n\nThis keeps the existing DeepEP waterfill behavior intact: waterfill construction first reduces `self.topk` to routed width, then its balancer expands the shared column exactly once.\n\nThe separate fused JIT hash-topk zero-token kernel launch failure described in the issue is outside this change.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `PYTHONPATH=python:. pytest -q test/registered/moe/test_hash_topk.py` — 4 passed\n- `ruff check python/sglang/srt/layers/moe/hash_topk.py test/registered/moe/test_hash_topk.py`\n- `python -m py_compile python/sglang/srt/layers/moe/hash_topk.py test/registered/moe/test_hash_topk.py`\n- confirmed the new regression cases both fail against unmodified main\n- separately exercised the waterfill routed-width-to-total-width empty expansion\n\nFixes #25919\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #30581947630](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30581947630)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #30581947139](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30581947139)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
